  {
   "id": "n02_forward_rays",
   "model": "neat",
   "title": "16 forward rays instead of 32 all around",
   "why": "The original lidar fans 32 rays over 324° centred on the car's right side: 13 point backwards and there is a\n36° blind gap on the left. In n00 the forward rays (about ±45°) carried most of the signal, and the side and\nback rays barely changed. Here: 16 rays over ±120° around the nose. Half the inputs, no blind spot, and a\nsmaller network to evolve. Everything else as n01.",
   "outcome": "Finishes all five tracks with half the inputs and in 47 minutes, a fifth of n00's training time. Laps are slower than n00 (23.2 s vs 20.9 s): it runs wide onto the grass on tracks 21 and 55 and loses 4-5 s there. Training episodes stop at 1000 frames (20 s), so a lap that long never finished during training.",
